Item 09 is complete and the gate passed. Recap:

**Delivered.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Pathwidth.lean` closes the development. The two cited results are named `Prop`s (`CubicPathwidthBound τ` for Fomin & Høie's cubic base case, `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ` for the Kneis et al. reduction lemma), quoted from the sources in their docstrings and never asserted. On top of them the file proves Lemma 5.1 and Corollary 5.2 of Edwards & McDermid: 21 theorems, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, every one on the standard three axioms. The final theorems carry exactly four hypotheses beyond the graph's own: the two `Prop`s, `Monotone τ` and `0 ≤ τ n`. Non-negativity of `ρ` is derived from (H3), and monotonicity of `ρ` turned out unnecessary because every reduction is on the ambient vertex type.

**Checked before stated.** Every deterministic lemma of the file was brute-forced on all 13,598 graphs to 8 vertices in the form Lean proves it, including the deletion lemma on every vertex subset and the component inclusion on every connected subset, plus the item's numerical pin on 500 random graphs to 12 vertices. Zero violations.

**Records.** 21 axiom lines added (577 checked, 0 failures), the sandwich audit extended (371 names; 22 rows, 5,793 checks, 0 violations), 3 new tests (50 in the module), report §9 with the proved/cited table and the two Appendix A rows drafted for item 10, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md updated. Gate: lake build ok, 1,799 and 123 tests passed, paper check ok at 74 pages.

